SolarX AR orbit-data mirror
===========================

The file published at https://dunyakilavuz.com/solarx-data/v1/orbits.json
contains third-party data, republished unchanged except for filtering:

1. Satellite orbital elements (GP data, TLE format), CelesTrak groups
   "stations" and "visual":
   CelesTrak, Dr. T.S. Kelso, https://celestrak.org
   https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php?GROUP=stations&FORMAT=tle
   https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php?GROUP=visual&FORMAT=tle
   The GP data originate from the 18th Space Defense Squadron, U.S. Space
   Force, and are published via https://www.space-track.org. USSPACECOM has
   given "express blanket approval for transfer/redistribution of basic SSA
   data ... conditioned on appropriate citation" (basic SSA data include
   TLEs/OMMs): https://www.space-track.org/documentation
   Downloads follow CelesTrak's usage policy (https://celestrak.org/usage-policy.php):
   at most one download per group per run, two runs a day, no retries, and
   any non-200 answer stops the download.

2. Comet and minor-planet orbits:
   IAU Minor Planet Center, https://minorplanetcenter.net
   /iau/MPCORB/CometEls.txt and /iau/Ephemerides/Bright/<year>/Soft00Bright.txt
   MPC website use policy (https://www.minorplanetcenter.net/iau/WWWPolicy.html):
   "Data files are copyrighted entities and may be redistributed as long as
   the source for the data is clearly specified."
   This product has made use of data and/or services provided by the
   International Astronomical Union's Minor Planet Center.

The same credits are included in the published JSON ("sources") and in the
SolarX AR app.
